# Supabase Skills (Cotarco)

Official docs: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/getting-started/ai-skills  
Upstream: https://github.com/supabase/agent-skills

Repo skills (`.agents/skills/`): `supabase`, `supabase-postgres-best-practices`.

## Mandatory before DB / Auth / Storage / Supabase-backed API

Follow `cotarco-commercial-manager/agents.md` §5.3:

1. Read `.agents/skills/supabase/SKILL.md`
2. Read `.agents/skills/supabase-postgres-best-practices/SKILL.md`
3. Load relevant `references/` (priority: `query-*`, `security-*`, `schema-*`, `conn-*`)
4. Apply Supabase security checklist (RLS on exposed schemas, no `service_role` in clients, no `user_metadata` for authz, views/`SECURITY DEFINER` caution)
5. Verify with a real test query after changes
6. Handoff: `SUPABASE_SKILLS_USED`

Phases `02-database` and `03-api` always load both skills (matrix §11).

## Hard rules

- Do not invent Supabase APIs from training data — verify changelog/docs when unsure
- Enable RLS on every table in exposed schemas; pair `GRANT` with policies
- Never commit secrets or put `service_role` in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`
- Prefer Supabase MCP tools when available for project inspection/migrations

## Refresh

```bash
npx skills add supabase/agent-skills
```

If the CLI fails, re-copy from a clone of `supabase/agent-skills` into `.agents/skills/` (see each skill's `SOURCE.md`).
